# Reviewed production deployment state for the self-serve lead funnel.
# Activation is a code-reviewed change from dormant to active; the build guard
# then requires the Actions-provided VITE_API_BASE_URL to be HTTPS and CSP-safe.
#
# HISTORY. Activated on 2026-08-04 (#245) before its prod dependencies were
# ready, then reverted to dormant on 2026-08-05 (#247): the edge (Cloudflare)
# CSP did not allow `api.traigent.ai` in connect-src, and `POST /api/v1/leads`
# returned 404. An active funnel therefore hard-failed the "Connect your agent"
# button instead of falling back to the HubSpot capture.
#
# The revert named two conditions for re-activation. As measured on 2026-08-06:
#   1. Edge CSP — DONE. The live `content-security-policy` response header on
#      both traigent.ai and www.traigent.ai now lists https://api.traigent.ai in
#      connect-src.
#   2. Backend lead route live — the routes are REGISTERED on prod (`GET
#      /api/v1/leads` and `/api/v1/leads/verify` answer 405 Method Not Allowed,
#      while an unknown path answers 401), but they are still gated off by
#      `ENABLE_LEAD_ACCESS_ONBOARDING`, which the prod deployment does not set.
#      While the flag is off, lead_routes.py answers POST with a generic 404 by
#      design. traigent-iac#406 adds the flag and the three lead secret
#      references, and ArgoCD syncs traigent-iac `main` automatically
#      (`automated` + `selfHeal`, plugin `cuelang`, ENVNAME=main), so merging
#      #406 is itself the deploy — no separate apply step to wait for.
#
# MERGE GATE for this change — check the behaviour, not the PR state:
#   curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}\n' -X POST https://api.traigent.ai/api/v1/leads \
#     -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"email":"<a mailbox you own>","website":"","elapsed_seconds":9}'
#   # 404 -> flag still off, DO NOT MERGE.  202 -> enabled; a code e-mail is on its way.
VITE_FUNNEL_STATE=active
